{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507447604,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNDk4ODU1Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/860#issuecomment-334988552"},"message":"With #1630 the metadata parser can now be instructed with files to care about, but there is no concept of incremental metadata updates WITHIN a dataset (just across). At the same time the potential runtime delay can only go up with more and more complex parsers. OTOH `save` is called ALL the time. I am 100% confident that nobody wants to pay this price -- in general.\n\nIf desired in some specific scenario though, the `--run-after` config switch could be used to run metadata aggregation after `save()`. `aggregate-metadata` will not alter a dataset unless metadata-relevant pieces have changed. It probably won't work out of the box right now, but in principle this is the way I would achieve this.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1507447604,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTI4MzEwMDY3OQ=="},"status":2},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1507472768,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNTAxMDE2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/860#issuecomment-335010160"},"message":"Aggregate-metadata isn't a plugin, but a command ;-) (still not sure what is the fundamental difference besides the visibility etc). I think we will keep running into this until there would be more automagic solution, so I would prefer to keep this one open","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1507472768,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEzOlJlb3BlbmVkRXZlbnQxMjgzMTk5MTcy"},"status":1},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1523015651,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3OTIzMTEzMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/860#issuecomment-379231132"},"message":"I will close this now (again). Full aggregation can take forever, partial re-aggregation is pretty much fiction with the current setup. A different bu related issue is: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2341\n\nSure thing, more complex solutions are possible, but I will not work on this, not did anyone else over the past to years.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1523015651,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTU2MDc0MzUzMw=="},"status":2}]}